      "artist": "Hugh Llewelyn",
      "credit": "Robert Stephenson &amp; Hawthorn 7284\n\nUploaded by Oxyman",
      "source": "Robert Stephenson & Hawthorn 7284 (6250860062)",
      "description": "Robert Stephenson &amp; Hawthorn 550 v dc overhead Bo-Bo No.7284 of 1945, \"Doug Tottman\", one of four built for Kearsley Power Station, Lancashire 1928-45. First named \"Kearsley No.4\", it was the RSH continuation of a Hawthron Leslie design (see No.3682 \"Kearsley Power Station No.1\"). It was used there until 1982 when the CEGB rebuilt it as a battery loco and moved it to Heysham Nuclear Power Station where it was named \"Heysham No.1\". British Energy withdrew it in 2009. In preservation it was renamed \"Doug Tottman\". At the Electric Railway Museum, Coventry, 9/11.",
      "dateCreated": "2011-09-10 10:26",
