      "source": "English Electric E905 (6243717021)",
      "description": "English Electric Type 3B, 200 v dc overhead &amp; battery, 35 hp 0-4-0 No.E905 of 1935, \"Spondon No.1\". The Type 3B was a standard EE type in the 1920's &amp; 30's. It was built for the Derbyshire &amp; Nottinghamshire Electric Power Company for use at their Spondon Power Staion, Derbs., one of 3 used there. It was withdrawn in 1984 - a long working life. At the Electric Railway Museum, Coventry, 9/11.",
